d house flipping be a good  option listen  saving money i don't believe in saving  money i believe in storing money now the  difference between saving money and  storing money  saving money is when you just save it  for a rainy day or you just put it away  and you save it up in the bank you lock  it away in the bank  that's not smart because money is  shrinking storing  money is when you store it with a view  to  invest it so i would i would get 100 i  would save money or store money  and house flipping would that be a good  option maybe  i mean if you're 17 i would be more  inclined to just try and get yourself  on the ladder on the ladder get your  foot in the door  if you buy a house and sell it it's a  lot of work and then you lose the house  and the profit that you get you have to  pay tax on  so you're probably better off buying it  pushing it up and instead of selling it  refinancing it and then any money that  you pull out is  tax free and you keep the house  which means you've got a house to your  portfolio that you can rent  so i'll probably do that but anyway good  luck  okay miles some firm says  i wanted to know how you work out the  occupation rate  in an area when doing rent to serviced  accommodation  right so if you're doing rent-to-service  accommodation  first thing i'll say is across the  country  you're talking about 75 to 85 percent  occupancy rate is about standard  so if you're renting a property out of  serviced accommodation  namely short staylets on booking.com and  airbnb  you're probably if it's a nice decent  house  you're probably going to be it's  probably going to be void about 20  of the time so that's just standard  however  what i would suggest that you do is look  on booking.com  and see how full the hotels are if you  can't book a hotel within the next three  days because everywhere's fully booked  and your property is in that area that's  a really good sign  if you're ringing up or ring up a hotel  and say hi i'm looking for um